# Force LF endings for shell scripts regardless of platform checkout
# settings. deploy/user-data.sh gets pasted verbatim into EC2's "User
# data" field and run by cloud-init on Linux -- a CRLF shebang line
# (`#!/bin/bash\r`) fails with "bad interpreter: No such file or
# directory" on Linux. Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) would
# otherwise silently convert this to CRLF on disk.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Source and config files: LF in the repo and in every checkout, whatever the
# platform's core.autocrlf says -- removes the "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warnings and mixed endings on Windows. Data files (CSV/TXT/JSON) and model
# artifacts are deliberately NOT listed: model_store hashes the training CSVs
# and reference-corpus ingest dedups on content hash, so their bytes are left
# exactly as they are.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
